Simpleton: a "dstdec_threads" option for the sacdiso and dsdiff decoder plugins.

The DST decoder (libdstdec, dst_engine_t) starts one worker thread per CPU
core (std::thread::hardware_concurrency()).  On the RGB20SX (RK3566, four
A55 cores, no heatsink) a DST-compressed SACD track lights all four cores at
1.8 GHz in bursts, the SoC reaches the TSADC's hardware thermal shutdown
(rockchip,hw-tshut-temp = 95 C) within seconds and the board resets with no
trace in any log (seen 11 Oct 2026, twice on one stereo track, once with the
DAC off; proven by capping the clock at 1104 MHz: the same track then peaks
at 78 C).  The plugin already declared param_dstdec_threads but never read it.

    decoder {
        plugin "sacdiso"
        playable_area "stereo"
        dstdec_threads "2"
    }

0 (the default) keeps the old behaviour: one thread per core.
The dst_decoder_t::init() signature gains the thread count (default 0) so
the other callers are unchanged.

